rt Schweitzer\n\n\n2. Users.txt\n   - Content Format: \n     \n     Username|Password\n\n   - Data Example:\n     \n     user1|abc123\n     user2|def456\n\n\n3. Favorites.txt\n   - Content Format: \n     \n     Username|Quote|Author\n\n   - Data Example:\n     \n     user1|The best way to predict the future is to invent it.|Alan Kay\n\n\nBy adhering to this requirements document, the development team will ensure a robust and user-friendly MotivationalQuotesApp.', 'requirements': '', 'composition': {'Programmer 1': "Implement the backend code in app.py to handle routing for all frontend pages and manage file read/write operations. The website should be accessible via the local port 5000, and the login page can be directly accessed through the route '/'. The backend code must implement routing for all frontend pages, ensuring that each route corresponds to the frontend code. File read and write operations in the backend code should start from the first line of the file, without any encryption, using plain text. The frontend code files include  login.html, home.html, add_quote.html, edit_quote.html, delete_confirmation.html, favorites.html, and about.html.", 'Programmer 2': 'Develop the login page frontend code in templates/login.html. The page should include a username input field, a password input field, a login button, and an about button. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 3': 'Develop the home page frontend code in templates/home.html. The page should display a welcome message, a section for displaying quotes with edit and delete options, an add quote button, and a favorites button. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 4': 'Develop the add quote page frontend code in templates/add_quote.html. The page should include a quote input field, an author input field, and a submit quote button. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 5': 'Develop the edit quote page frontend code in templates/edit_quote.html. The page should include a quote input field, an author input field, and an update quote button. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 6': 'Develop the delete confirmation page frontend code in templates/delete_confirmation.html. The page should include a confirmation message, a confirm deletion button, and a cancel button. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 7': 'Develop the favorites page frontend code in templates/favorites.html. The page should display all quotes marked as favorites. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.', 'Programmer 8': 'Develop the about page frontend code in templates/about.html. The page should include an application description and developer information. All URLs in the frontend code should be routes, not HTML file names.'}, 'workflow': {'Programmer 1': [], 'Programmer 2': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 3': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 4': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 5': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 6': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 7': ['Programmer 1'], 'Programmer 8': ['Programmer 1']}, 'codes': 'app.py\npython\n\'\'\'\nThis is the main application file for the MotivationalQuotesApp. It handles routing for all frontend pages and manages file read/write operations.\n\'\'\'\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for\nimport os\napp = Flask(__name__)\nDATA_DIR = \'data\'\nQUOTES_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \'Quotes.txt\')\nUSERS_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \'Users.txt\')\nFAVORITES_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \'Favorites.txt\')\ndef read_quotes():\n    quotes = []\n    with open(QUOTES_FILE, \'r\') as file:\n        for line in file:\n            quote, author = line.strip().split(\'|\')\n            quotes.append({\'quote\': quote, \'author\': author})\n    return quotes\ndef read_users():\n    users = {}\n    with open(USERS_FILE, \'r\') as file:\n        for line in file:\n            username, password = line.strip().split(\'|\')\n            users[username] = password\n    return users\ndef write_quote(quote, author):\n    with open(QUOTES_FILE, \'a\') as file:\n        file.write(f"{quote}|{author}\\n")\ndef delete_quote(quote):\n    quotes = read_quotes()\n    quotes = [q for q in quotes if q[\'quote\'] != quote]\n    with open(QUOTES_FILE, \'w\') as file:\n        for q in quotes:\n            file.write(f"{q[\'quote\']}|{q[\'author\']}\\n")\n@app.route(\'/\', methods=[\'GET\', \'POST\'])\ndef login():\n    if request.method == \'POST\':\n        username = request.form[\'username\']\n        password = request.form[\'password\']\n        users = read_users()\n        if username in users and users[username] == password:\n            return redirect(url_for(\'home\'))\n        else:\n            return render_template(\'login.html\', error="Invalid credentials")\n    return render_template(\'login.html\')\n@app.route(\'/home\')\ndef home():\n    quotes = read_quotes()\n    return render_template(\'home.html\', quotes=quotes)\n@app.route(\'/add_quote\', methods=[\'GET\', \'POST\'])\ndef add_quote():\n    if request.method == \'POST\':\n        quote = request.form[\'quote_input\']\n        author = request.form[\'author_input\']\n        write_quote(quote, author)\n        return redirect(url_for(\'home\'))\n    return render_template(\'add_quote.html\')\n@app.route(\'/edit_quote/&lt;quote_id&gt;\', methods=[\'GET\', \'POST\'])\ndef edit_quote(quote_id):\n    quotes = read_quotes()\n    if request.method == \'POST\':\n        updated_quote = request.form[\'edit_quote_input\']\n        updated_author = request.form[\'edit_author_input\']\n        delete_quote(quotes[int(quote_id)][\'quote\'])\n        write_quote(updated_quote, updated_author)\n        return redirect(url_for(\'home\'))\n    return render_template(\'edit_quote.html\', quote=quotes[int(quote_id)])\n@app.route(\'/delete_confirmation/&lt;quote_id&gt;\')\ndef delete_confirmation(quote_id):\n    quotes = read_quotes()\n    return render_template(\'delete_confirmation.html\', quote=quotes[int(quote_id)])\n@app.route(\'/confirm_deletion/&lt;quote_id&gt;\')\ndef confirm_deletion(quote_id):\n    quotes = read_quotes()\n    delete_quote(quotes[int(quote_id)][\'quote\'])\n    return redirect(url_for(\'home\'))\n@app.route(\'/favorites\')\ndef favorites():\n    # This function would need to read from the Favorites.txt file\n    # For now, we will just return an empty list\n    return render_template(\'favorites.html\', favorites=[])\n@app.route(\'/about\')\ndef about():\n    return render_template(\'about.html\')\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    app.run(port=5000)\n\n\nlogin.html\nhtml\n&lt;!--\nThis is the login page for the MotivationalQuotesApp. It allows users to enter their credentials to log in.\n--&gt;\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang="en"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Login&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Login&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;form action="{{ url_for(\'login\') }}" method="post"&gt;\n        &lt;label for="username_input"&gt;Username:&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type="text" id="username_input" name="username" required&gt;\n        &lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;label for="password_input"&gt;Password:&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type="password" id="password_input" name="password" required&gt;\n        &lt;br&gt;\n        &lt;button type="submit" id="login_button"&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    {% if error %}\n        &lt;p style="color:red;"&gt;{{ error }}&lt;/p&gt;\n    {% endif %}\n    &lt;button id="about_button" onclick="window.location.href=\'{{ url_for(\'about\') }}\'"&gt;About&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n\n\nhome.html\nhtml\n&lt;!--\nThis is the home page for the MotivationalQuotesApp. It displays a welcome message, a list of quotes with edit and delete options, and buttons to add quotes and view favorites.\n--&gt;\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang="en"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Home&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1 id="welcome_message"&gt;Welcome to Motivational Quotes App!&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Your Quotes&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;div id="quotes_display"&gt;\n        {% for quote in quotes %}\n            &lt;div id="quote_item_{{ loop.index0 }}"&gt;\n                &lt;p&gt;"{{ quote.quote }}" - {{ quote.author }}&lt;/p&gt;\n                &lt;button id="edit_quote_{{ loop.index0 }}" onclick="window.location.href=\'{{ url_for(\'edit_quote\', quote_id=loop.index0) }}\'"&gt;Edit&lt;/button&gt;\n                &lt;button id="delete_quote_{{ loop.index0 }}" onclick="window.location.href=\'{{ url_for(\'delete_confirmation\', quote_id=loop.index0) }}\'"&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;\n            &lt;/div&gt;\n        {% endfor %}\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;button id="add_quote_button" onclick="window.location.href=\'{{ url_for(\'add_quote\') }}\'"&gt;Add Quote&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button id="favorites_button" onclick="window.location.href=\'{{ url_for(\'favorites\') }}\'"&gt;Favorites&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n\n\nadd_quote.html\nhtml\n&lt;!--\nThis is the add quote page for the MotivationalQuotesApp. It allows users to input a new quote and author to submit.\n--&gt;\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang="en"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Add Quote&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Add a New Quote&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;form action="{{ url_for(\'add_quote\') }}" method="post"&gt;\n        &lt;label for="quote_input"&gt;Quo